  "prefLabel": "He-P 2306.04 Request for an Administrative Hearing",
  "priorExpiration": "2019-08-20",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-P 2306.04 Request for an Administrative Hearing.\n\n(a) An applicant or licensee shall have 10 calendar days after receipt of the notice of an enforcement action to request in writing a hearing to contest the action.\n\n(b) If a written request for a hearing is not received pursuant to (a) above, the applicant or licensee waives his right to a hearing and the action of the department shall become final.\n\n(c) Hearings under this section shall be conducted in accordance with RSA 541-A and He-C 200.\n\n(d) For administrative fines, the fines shall be paid to the department no later than 30 days from the receipt of the notice, unless a hearing has been requested.\n\nSource. #6722, eff 3-27-98; ss by #7893, eff 5-21-03; ss by #9857-A, eff 2-1-11, EXPIRED: 2-1-19\n\nNew. #12729, INTERIM, eff 2-21-19, EXPIRES: 8-20-19; ss by #12852, eff 8-20-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-p2300.html"
